    "background_story": "Philip was a renowned botanist who spent his life studying the unique flora of the Andes mountains. His latest obsession was the Bomarea, a genus of flowering plants found only in the remote regions of South America. Philip's quest to catalog and preserve these rare species took him to the most inhospitable terrain, where he braved treacherous paths and unpredictable weather. His dedication paid off when he discovered a new species of Bomarea, which he named Bomarea philippi in honor of his grandfather, a fellow botanist. Philip's groundbreaking research shed new light on the importance of preserving these delicate flowers and their habitats. His work inspired a new generation of botanists and conservationists, cementing his legacy as a leading authority on the Bomarea genus.",
